  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"Every table has a willing teacher and printed rule aids; the explanation covers all essential rules before the main game begins.\", \"decision\": \"How should the main rules explanation be delivered?\", \"goal\": \"Help guests find compatible games, understand how to play, and enjoy the evening without avoidable waiting or confusion.\", \"problem\": \"A community room is hosting an evening of board games for adults with different levels of experience. Several tables, a host, willing game teachers, short waiting activities, and a varied collection are available. Guests can decline any game and join a later one. Every game has an agreed latest stopping time before the room closes, and ordinary refreshments and conversation have their own small areas.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nThe teacher demonstrates essential rules with the components while players follow the printed aid and ask questions as they arise. The table connects written instructions to visible actions before attempting the game themselves.\nPlayers read the printed rule aid first, and the teacher checks essential rules through a short table discussion. The conversation concentrates on gaps in understanding after each player has had time to inspect the instructions.\nThe teacher explains the essential rules to the whole table using the printed aid before taking questions. Everyone hears the same starting account, and questions can refer back to a shared explanation."
    }
  ],
